{"at":"2026-11-01T15:44:39.536Z","type":"result","sequence":2,"path":"/Users/pelicannurse/.t3/projects/first-person-shooter-soul-game/docs/media/build41-review2/how-to.jpg","captureMs":107.95275000000038,"beforePause":{"phase":"dialog","dialog":"OPERATOR HANDBOOK\n×\nMOVE WITH PURPOSE.\n\nExtraction uploads only while standing inside the marked uplink deck. Outside pauses briefly; reenter before decay.\n\nEngineering has two single-use amber capacitor banks. Shoot the cabinet or isolator: a 1.1-second warning precedes a 6 m discharge. Move clear, use solid cover or phase protection. The spent cabinet remains cover. Enemy fire cannot trigger it.\n\nW A S D\nMove\nMOUSE\nLook\nLMB\nFire coil rifle\nRMB\nAim down sights\nR\nReload\nSHIFT\nSoul Shift / dash\nCTRL\nSprint\nSPACE\nJump\nHOLD E\nRecover nearby memory\nM\nFacility map · mission paused\nESC\nPause / release mouse\n\nSoul Shift protects briefly. Dash within 4.5 m of a charging enemy to cancel its shot and stagger it for 0.8 s. A blue emitter flash confirms the break. Dashing toward a charge stops early on a successful break so you can follow up. Sideways dodges retain full travel. It deals no damage; the 4.5 s cooldown still applies. Your shield regenerates when you avoid damage.\n\nTHREAT VISOR · Orange ! means a charging threat. Muted chevrons show recent fire or hits. A number counts nearby sources in that direction; one source has no number. Offscreen cues use broad direction sectors, not exact positions. Optic brackets stay beside visible emitters. The lower readout follows one target near aim. Cues require clear optic sight and expire.\n\nUNDERSTOOD\n↗"},"after":{"phase":"dialog","dialog":"OPERATOR HANDBOOK\n×\nMOVE WITH PURPOSE.\n\nExtraction uploads only while standing inside the marked uplink deck. Outside pauses briefly; reenter before decay.\n\nEngineering has two single-use amber capacitor banks. Shoot the cabinet or isolator: a 1.1-second warning precedes a 6 m discharge. Move clear, use solid cover or phase protection. The spent cabinet remains cover. Enemy fire cannot trigger it.\n\nW A S D\nMove\nMOUSE\nLook\nLMB\nFire coil rifle\nRMB\nAim down sights\nR\nReload\nSHIFT\nSoul Shift / dash\nCTRL\nSprint\nSPACE\nJump\nHOLD E\nRecover nearby memory\nM\nFacility map · mission paused\nESC\nPause / release mouse\n\nSoul Shift protects briefly. Dash within 4.5 m of a charging enemy to cancel its shot and stagger it for 0.8 s. A blue emitter flash confirms the break. Dashing toward a charge stops early on a successful break so you can follow up. Sideways dodges retain full travel. It deals no damage; the 4.5 s cooldown still applies. Your shield regenerates when you avoid damage.\n\nTHREAT VISOR · Orange ! means a charging threat. Muted chevrons show recent fire or hits. A number counts nearby sources in that direction; one source has no number. Offscreen cues use broad direction sectors, not exact positions. Optic brackets stay beside visible emitters. The lower readout follows one target near aim. Cues require clear optic sight and expire.\n\nUNDERSTOOD\n↗"},"clientMs":172.22262499999852,"pageErrors":[]}
